Package: qesR
Type: Package
Title: Access Quebec Election Study Datasets
Version: 0.9.1
Maintainer: Thomas Gareau-Paquette <tg454@cornell.edu>
Authors@R:
    person(
      given = "Thomas",
      family = "Gareau-Paquette",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      email = "tg454@cornell.edu"
    )
Description: Load the Quebec Election Studies and related Quebec election
    surveys from their 'Dataverse' deposits ('Borealis' and the 'Harvard
    Dataverse') by study code. Each study is pinned to one dataset version and
    one original 'SPSS' or 'Stata' data file, checked by its 'MD5' checksum
    before use. An offline catalog lists the studies, their documents and their
    citations, and shipped metadata give codebooks, question wording and search
    in English and French without network access. An experimental engine
    harmonizes selected variables across studies from a versioned specification
    whose rows record their review status (the legacy master also applies rows
    still in review), with each study's waves, weights and comparability grades,
    and returns survey designs for the 'survey' and 'srvyr' packages. Data come
    from the Quebec Election Studies of 2007 (Bélanger et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/6XGOKA>, 2008 (Bélanger and Nadeau 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/8KEYU3>, 2012 (Bélanger et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/WXUPXT>, 2014 (Bélanger and Nadeau 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/64F7WR>, 2018 (Bélanger et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/NWTGWS> and 2022 (Mahéo et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.7910/DVN/PAQBDR>; the panel surveys on the 2007 and 2012 Quebec
    elections (Durand and Goyder 2023) <doi:10.5683/SP3/NDS6VT>
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/RKHPVL> and on the 2018 election (Durand and Blais 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/XDDMMR>; the 'CROP' polls of 2007-2010 (Durand 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/IRZ1PF>; and the 1998 election polls (Durand 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/QFUAWG>. The studies are catalogued by the Centre for the
    Study of Democratic Citizenship
    <https://csdc-cecd.ca/portail-quebecois-sur-lopinion-publique/>. The MIT
    licence covers the package code only: the metadata shipped for the 2022
    study keep its licence, CC BY-NC 4.0 (see the file COPYRIGHTS).
